      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is probably gonna be quite confusing that the function is \"host_donate_hyp\" while the host page state becomes SHARED_OWNED. So maybe explain why we are doing it this way, i.e. that for \"simplicity\" (or more precisely, to minimize changes to the already overcomplicated implementation of memory protection API in v6.12), donation is actually implemented via sharing + pinning, so the host formally remains the \"owner\" of the pages, but in fact the host has only read access to them, while the hypervisor has full access (so essentially the end result is the same as if the pages were actually donated to the hypervisor and then shared read-only with the host)?",
      "revId": "3034d4e62fe592b9fa62d8f842e0c4e8534d36b0",
